WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.345 --> 00:00:01.178
- Want to see something cool?

00:00:01.178 --> 00:00:03.047
Ready for this?

00:00:03.047 --> 00:00:03.988
- That wasn't cool.

00:00:03.988 --> 00:00:05.613
- Do it in slow-mo and it's cool.

00:00:05.613 --> 00:00:07.196
Do that in slow-mo.

00:00:11.346 --> 00:00:13.631
- Today we are on our way to Las Vegas,

00:00:13.631 --> 00:00:15.232
and what is Vegas known for?

00:00:15.232 --> 00:00:16.065
Buffets.

00:00:16.065 --> 00:00:18.703
So we are going to go to three
drastically different buffets

00:00:18.703 --> 00:00:20.714
at three drastically
different price points

00:00:20.714 --> 00:00:22.398
to find out which one's the most worth it

00:00:22.398 --> 00:00:23.400
at its price.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.904
- The last time you went to Vegas

00:00:24.904 --> 00:00:27.028
you were in different company.

00:00:27.028 --> 00:00:29.047
- Keith and Steven, best buddies for life.

00:00:29.047 --> 00:00:30.318
I have matured a lot now.

00:00:30.318 --> 00:00:32.390
I'm not just going to be
screaming out Vegas, baby.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.560
- It will be my first time ever.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.393
- What?

00:00:34.393 --> 00:00:35.905
- Should I scream out Vegas, baby?

00:00:35.905 --> 00:00:37.765
- Usually when people are in
Vegas they're intoxicated.

00:00:37.765 --> 00:00:38.964
When they're intoxicated
they just want to eat

00:00:38.964 --> 00:00:39.806
a lot of food.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:43.109
We're going to find out how
good the food is unintoxicated.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.916
I mean, if there's a drinks buffet

00:00:44.916 --> 00:00:46.825
maybe we'll partake a little.

00:00:46.825 --> 00:00:48.432
We have to have the full experience.

00:00:48.432 --> 00:00:49.387
We've got to do our jobs here.

00:00:49.387 --> 00:00:51.387
- Okay, so Vegas.
- Baby.

00:00:52.577 --> 00:00:54.516
- You said we're in Vegas.
- Baby.

00:00:54.516 --> 00:00:56.435
- I know you like to
have an occasional drink.

00:00:56.435 --> 00:00:57.593
I like to have a good time.

00:00:57.593 --> 00:00:59.502
- Adam is a good time.

00:00:59.502 --> 00:01:00.588
- And that's Vegas.

00:01:00.588 --> 00:01:04.855
- Baby, it's not about the
destination, yada yada.

00:01:04.855 --> 00:01:06.076
(tongue vibration)

00:01:06.076 --> 00:01:09.743
(lively instrumental music)

00:01:10.697 --> 00:01:13.652
- My name is Timothy Radigan
and I'm the Executive Chef

00:01:13.652 --> 00:01:16.000
for the Feast Buffet here at Red Rock.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.287
We do breakfast, lunch, and dinner.

00:01:17.287 --> 00:01:18.262
Today we have breakfast out.

00:01:18.262 --> 00:01:20.113
We do omelets, we do scrambled eggs,

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.526
we carve bone-in ham.

00:01:21.526 --> 00:01:22.774
Our dessert station is open.

00:01:22.774 --> 00:01:24.086
We have breakfast pastries.

00:01:24.086 --> 00:01:26.847
I mean we have 154 items
available for breakfast.

00:01:26.847 --> 00:01:28.637
Almost everything here
is made from scratch,

00:01:28.637 --> 00:01:30.080
which you rarely find at a buffet.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.640
Feast Buffet has always been
behind supporting locals.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.261
We try and keep things changing
just so there's variety

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.352
for people who come a few times a week.

00:01:37.352 --> 00:01:38.418
- How do you keep all the food fresh?

00:01:38.418 --> 00:01:40.572
- With the sheer numbers
that we do it's fantastic

00:01:40.572 --> 00:01:42.056
because the food goes.

00:01:42.056 --> 00:01:43.814
- How much is the breakfast buffet here?

00:01:43.814 --> 00:01:45.745
- Breakfast is $6.99 for club members

00:01:45.745 --> 00:01:47.776
and it's $8.99 without the card.

00:01:47.776 --> 00:01:48.609
- What?

00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:49.442
- That is crazy.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.275
- You ready?

00:01:50.275 --> 00:01:51.230
- Yeah, let's do it.

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:53.696
- We're going, Andrew, we're gone.

00:01:53.696 --> 00:01:54.673
Getting a plate.

00:01:54.673 --> 00:01:56.086
Usually we share a dish.

00:01:56.086 --> 00:01:57.314
- [Andrew] Yeah, but
now we're at a buffet.

00:01:57.314 --> 00:01:59.174
And buffets are not about sharing.

00:01:59.174 --> 00:02:00.928
- [Steven] Because I was in
charge of making my plate

00:02:00.928 --> 00:02:03.356
I kind of threw balance out the window.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.542
Got an eggs bene, jelly donut, jell-o.

00:02:05.542 --> 00:02:07.472
It's about variety of experience.

00:02:07.472 --> 00:02:09.159
I want as many different
textures happening

00:02:09.159 --> 00:02:10.683
on my plate as possible.

00:02:10.683 --> 00:02:12.520
- Not only did you get an eggs benedict,

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.682
but you also got an omelet
that's half the size

00:02:14.682 --> 00:02:15.570
of your plate.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:16.403
What's with that?

00:02:16.403 --> 00:02:17.236
- I like eggs.

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:18.281
- You've got to stay loose.

00:02:18.281 --> 00:02:19.794
What just came out?

00:02:19.794 --> 00:02:21.157
What's looking good?

00:02:21.157 --> 00:02:22.153
- [Steven] So I got the ham.

00:02:22.153 --> 00:02:25.149
- I forgot about the carved him.

00:02:25.149 --> 00:02:26.806
Oh (bleep) you got the hash brown.

00:02:26.806 --> 00:02:28.249
I'm going to be having
some of your hash browns.

00:02:28.249 --> 00:02:29.508
- Get off of my hash browns.

00:02:29.508 --> 00:02:30.512
Can we cheers plates?

00:02:30.512 --> 00:02:31.987
- Yeah, we can cheers plates.

00:02:31.987 --> 00:02:35.725
- All right, grab hold of your pancake.

00:02:35.725 --> 00:02:37.246
- You can't even see
your red velvet pancake.

00:02:37.246 --> 00:02:39.310
- [Steven] It's in there.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:41.037
- It's covered by a waffle.

00:02:41.037 --> 00:02:43.353
- No, no, no, it's topped with a waffle.

00:02:43.353 --> 00:02:44.735
- I'm going to go for my French toast,

00:02:44.735 --> 00:02:46.534
since that's the closest thing I have

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:48.331
to a red velvet pancake.

00:02:48.331 --> 00:02:49.414
- Here we go.

00:02:53.016 --> 00:02:53.849
Whoa.

00:02:53.849 --> 00:02:54.986
- [Andrew] It's so fluffy.

00:02:54.986 --> 00:02:55.819
- That's was delicious.

00:02:55.819 --> 00:02:57.201
That's probably the best
thing that they have here.

00:02:57.201 --> 00:02:58.632
- Start with a little eggy action.

00:02:58.632 --> 00:03:01.752
- [Steven] Oh yeah,
I'll eat eggs with you.

00:03:01.752 --> 00:03:03.488
- These are actually
very good scrambled eggs.

00:03:03.488 --> 00:03:05.804
Mass produced scrambled
eggs are usually among

00:03:05.804 --> 00:03:07.673
the worst foods, but these are great.

00:03:07.673 --> 00:03:08.506
- These are not powder eggs.

00:03:08.506 --> 00:03:10.071
- No, they're cracking eggs back there.

00:03:10.071 --> 00:03:11.699
I saw a big ol' bowl of eggs.

00:03:11.699 --> 00:03:13.455
- Look at how thick that ham steak is.

00:03:13.455 --> 00:03:14.796
She just like gave me a ...

00:03:14.796 --> 00:03:16.513
- [Andrew] She carved you off a hunk.

00:03:16.513 --> 00:03:19.282
My college roommate
really loved ham steaks.

00:03:19.282 --> 00:03:21.574
Seeing that ham makes me think of him.

00:03:21.574 --> 00:03:22.407
- It's good ham.

00:03:22.407 --> 00:03:23.719
You want some omelet?

00:03:23.719 --> 00:03:25.400
- I'm good, I enjoy watching you.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.233
- It's fluffy.

00:03:26.233 --> 00:03:27.934
- Boom, we feasted.

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.229
You know what I like about buffets?

00:03:29.229 --> 00:03:30.993
It reminds me of weird family memories.

00:03:30.993 --> 00:03:33.433
- I don't go to buffet alone usually.

00:03:33.433 --> 00:03:34.569
Oh, I have been, actually.

00:03:34.569 --> 00:03:35.665
(laughs)

00:03:35.665 --> 00:03:36.498
Hey Adam.

00:03:39.564 --> 00:03:42.844
Guys, I'm drunk on buffets and
it's only the first buffet.

00:03:42.844 --> 00:03:43.987
- I paced myself.

00:03:43.987 --> 00:03:45.868
That's your problem, you went in too hard.

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:48.295
They were really moving food there.

00:03:48.295 --> 00:03:50.662
Nothing was really sitting
around, unless it's meant

00:03:50.662 --> 00:03:52.266
to sit around like jell-o.

00:03:52.266 --> 00:03:53.099
- You know what time it is.

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:53.938
Buffet fact.

00:03:53.938 --> 00:03:56.776
NASA says that the brightest
spot on Earth that you can see

00:03:56.776 --> 00:03:58.702
from space is the Las Vegas Strip.

00:03:58.702 --> 00:04:02.162
- Wow, how many of those
lights are buffets?

00:04:02.162 --> 00:04:03.554
Ooh, a helicopter.

00:04:03.554 --> 00:04:05.250
- Oh God. (laughs)

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:08.646
- (groans) We're actually
now on the Strip.

00:04:08.646 --> 00:04:10.687
This is where the tourists
are, where the magic happens.

00:04:10.687 --> 00:04:11.917
- So where are we going to next?

00:04:11.917 --> 00:04:13.378
- We'll first we're going to the bathroom

00:04:13.378 --> 00:04:14.783
because I'm going to go
take care of some business

00:04:14.783 --> 00:04:16.366
and unpack my body.

00:04:18.268 --> 00:04:19.158
- I hate you.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.144
- The next place we're
going is the Wicked Spoon.

00:04:21.144 --> 00:04:23.291
- Spoon is my favorite utensil.

00:04:23.291 --> 00:04:26.208
(funky jazz music)

00:04:28.217 --> 00:04:30.446
- Hey I'm Rhori, the Chef
de Cuisine at Wicked Spoon.

00:04:30.446 --> 00:04:32.777
We're here at our restaurant
now, it's dinner time.

00:04:32.777 --> 00:04:34.044
- [Steven] Wicked Spoon,
what does that mean?

00:04:34.044 --> 00:04:37.127
- It's us taking a kind
of different angle.

00:04:37.127 --> 00:04:38.467
It's something outside the box.

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.551
We have the frog legs and bone marrow.

00:04:40.551 --> 00:04:42.794
Certain things that you won't
see on the normal buffet.

00:04:42.794 --> 00:04:43.938
Just being wicked with it.

00:04:43.938 --> 00:04:45.733
- I noticed that the size of the plate

00:04:45.733 --> 00:04:47.253
if different than a normal buffet.

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:48.440
- That's the spoon part.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.449
Everything's cooked to order, basically.

00:04:50.449 --> 00:04:52.741
We set these up and they're
little individual dishes.

00:04:52.741 --> 00:04:55.089
It's already plated for
you which makes it cleaner,

00:04:55.089 --> 00:04:57.628
but helps you not overeat
and us to alleviate

00:04:57.628 --> 00:04:58.812
the waste as well.

00:04:58.812 --> 00:05:00.299
- I mean, you're not going
to be able to stop him

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:01.797
from overeating, never stop eating.

00:05:01.797 --> 00:05:03.967
- Let's not forgot who
almost wrecked themselves

00:05:03.967 --> 00:05:05.300
at brunch today.

00:05:06.295 --> 00:05:08.237
What's the thing you're
most excited to try?

00:05:08.237 --> 00:05:09.714
Because we've got a lot to cover here.

00:05:09.714 --> 00:05:10.821
- [Steven] First it was the pork belly.

00:05:10.821 --> 00:05:13.663
But for me, it's the
bourbon glazed baby carrots.

00:05:13.663 --> 00:05:15.112
Never been excited to
eat carrots in my life.

00:05:15.112 --> 00:05:15.945
What about you?

00:05:15.945 --> 00:05:18.318
- [Andrew] Frog legs,
grits, whole crawfish.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:21.695
- Bone marrow, anything goes
here at the Wicked Spoon.

00:05:21.695 --> 00:05:24.841
So, first things first, I'm the realist.

00:05:24.841 --> 00:05:27.422
We were recommended to
get Wicked Margaritas.

00:05:27.422 --> 00:05:30.167
Wicked means good in this
context for those who are not

00:05:30.167 --> 00:05:32.661
up with the times, like
this kid right here.

00:05:32.661 --> 00:05:33.678
Was born in 1990.

00:05:33.678 --> 00:05:34.511
- Such a baby.

00:05:34.511 --> 00:05:35.882
- When were you born?

00:05:35.882 --> 00:05:36.715
- 1990.

00:05:39.954 --> 00:05:41.368
- This is too easy to drink.

00:05:41.368 --> 00:05:42.552
- (foreign words) Steven.

00:05:42.552 --> 00:05:43.698
Did you see the duck heads?

00:05:43.698 --> 00:05:45.781
They're not just bringing
duck meat in this place.

00:05:45.781 --> 00:05:46.965
They're bringing ducks.

00:05:46.965 --> 00:05:51.132
- Umm, that pork belly, so
rich and fatty and delicious.

00:05:52.291 --> 00:05:53.461
- Oh my God.

00:05:53.461 --> 00:05:54.570
- No, that pork belly
was better than whatever

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:55.425
you just put in your mouth?

00:05:55.425 --> 00:05:56.925
- You wanna wager?

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:01.103
- That actually is way
better than the pork belly

00:06:01.103 --> 00:06:01.936
I just ate.

00:06:01.936 --> 00:06:03.481
- Boom, touchdown.

00:06:03.481 --> 00:06:05.139
I actually never had a frog leg before.

00:06:05.139 --> 00:06:08.030
What's a high five called
if you use your foot?

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:09.280
Frog foot five.

00:06:10.601 --> 00:06:14.098
- Mm, technically we just
knocked the thighs together.

00:06:14.098 --> 00:06:16.052
I've had a lot of frog leg in my life.

00:06:16.052 --> 00:06:16.885
- Have you?

00:06:16.885 --> 00:06:17.856
- It's a very classic Chinese dish.

00:06:17.856 --> 00:06:19.425
But I've never had Buffalo frog legs.

00:06:19.425 --> 00:06:20.841
- That's good Buffalo sauce.

00:06:20.841 --> 00:06:22.547
It's actually got a nice heat to it.

00:06:22.547 --> 00:06:26.619
Wow, you just, where did that
bone come out of your mouth?

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:29.290
You were like storing it
back there like a squirrel

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:31.068
getting ready for winter.

00:06:31.068 --> 00:06:32.338
- What is the appropriate way to eat this?

00:06:32.338 --> 00:06:33.191
- Bone marrow?
- Yeah.

00:06:33.191 --> 00:06:35.556
- If you want to suck on
the bone and know you're ...

00:06:35.556 --> 00:06:36.775
- Bone sucker.

00:06:36.775 --> 00:06:38.029
These are really good.

00:06:38.029 --> 00:06:39.492
(laughing)

00:06:39.492 --> 00:06:41.308
- (bleep) I had a fortune cookie.

00:06:41.308 --> 00:06:43.943
Your health is important,
eat your vegetables.

00:06:43.943 --> 00:06:44.880
- Baby carrots.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:48.087
(lively jazz music)

00:06:48.087 --> 00:06:49.038
Mm, bourbon glaze.

00:06:49.038 --> 00:06:51.817
Yeah, these Marker's
Mark is not cheap whiskey

00:06:51.817 --> 00:06:53.706
and it's not a whiskey
that you would expect

00:06:53.706 --> 00:06:55.329
someone to cooked with.

00:06:55.329 --> 00:06:57.082
- It wasn't overcooked,
so you got that crunch.

00:06:57.082 --> 00:07:00.012
- Right, not only is that a nice glaze,

00:07:00.012 --> 00:07:01.762
the carrot flavor is not missing.

00:07:01.762 --> 00:07:02.595
- What is this?

00:07:02.595 --> 00:07:03.428
- That's carrot cake.

00:07:03.428 --> 00:07:06.987
I've had a carrot cake
every birthday of my life.

00:07:06.987 --> 00:07:09.599
(smooth jazz music)

00:07:09.599 --> 00:07:10.759
Very good carrot cake.

00:07:10.759 --> 00:07:14.318
For the amount and range
of stuff you get here.

00:07:14.318 --> 00:07:15.645
- There's the crab, there's duck.

00:07:15.645 --> 00:07:17.496
- The pork belly, the prime rib.

00:07:17.496 --> 00:07:19.585
- I know I say this every episode,

00:07:19.585 --> 00:07:21.545
but for real, this is the place I'm going

00:07:21.545 --> 00:07:22.378
to bring my girlfriend.

00:07:22.378 --> 00:07:24.946
It's really hard to beat this.

00:07:24.946 --> 00:07:26.808
That was the perfect buffet.

00:07:26.808 --> 00:07:27.641
- Really.

00:07:27.641 --> 00:07:30.116
- The food was super unique,
the chef was awesome.

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:31.993
- There were things that
I'd never had before,

00:07:31.993 --> 00:07:35.002
and I didn't expect to
try new food at a buffet.

00:07:35.002 --> 00:07:38.391
- I've got to say I was
wowed in the colon-O face.

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:40.061
- Not like the colon of your body?

00:07:40.061 --> 00:07:41.741
- I was going to say
colon-D face, but that's.

00:07:41.741 --> 00:07:43.619
- Neither is good.

00:07:43.619 --> 00:07:45.058
- Buffet fact.

00:07:45.058 --> 00:07:47.251
There was a study done, so one
group had four dollar buffet,

00:07:47.251 --> 00:07:49.070
the other group had eight dollar buffet.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:51.857
And the people who paid
eight dollars actually said

00:07:51.857 --> 00:07:54.112
that the pizza tastes
better than the people

00:07:54.112 --> 00:07:57.062
who paid four dollars, even
though it was exact same.

00:07:57.062 --> 00:07:59.051
- So you're saying lying works.

00:07:59.051 --> 00:08:01.815
If Vegas has taught me anything,
it's that blowing money

00:08:01.815 --> 00:08:03.903
can be pleasurable in itself.

00:08:03.903 --> 00:08:06.341
Hey, if a buffet tastes
better because I'm splurging

00:08:06.341 --> 00:08:07.974
a little more money on it,

00:08:07.974 --> 00:08:09.875
that's just a better buffet, sorry.

00:08:09.875 --> 00:08:12.899
- We woke up this morning
at 8:30 to go to one

00:08:12.899 --> 00:08:15.532
of the most classic buffets in Las Vegas.

00:08:15.532 --> 00:08:16.839
- We're going to the Sterling Brunch,

00:08:16.839 --> 00:08:18.761
which is only on Sundays.

00:08:18.761 --> 00:08:19.785
- It's a pretty special thing.

00:08:19.785 --> 00:08:20.618
- I'm ready.

00:08:20.618 --> 00:08:23.951
(light classical music)

00:08:27.211 --> 00:08:28.769
- Hi, I'm Elizabeth Braden-Watkins,

00:08:28.769 --> 00:08:30.842
I am the Assistant Executive
Chef of Bally's Paris

00:08:30.842 --> 00:08:31.892
of Planet Hollywood.

00:08:31.892 --> 00:08:33.369
We're here at Sterling Brunch of Bally's.

00:08:33.369 --> 00:08:35.319
This brunch is actually a Vegas tradition.

00:08:35.319 --> 00:08:36.538
It's over 30 years old.

00:08:36.538 --> 00:08:40.011
- So has this always been
the premiere Vegas brunch?

00:08:40.011 --> 00:08:40.844
- It has.

00:08:40.844 --> 00:08:43.644
I think people have an expectation
of what Sterling Brunch

00:08:43.644 --> 00:08:44.477
is supposed to be.

00:08:44.477 --> 00:08:46.118
That's why you have the
champagne, and the caviar,

00:08:46.118 --> 00:08:46.951
and lobster.

00:08:46.951 --> 00:08:48.631
Right here is our fresh seafood station.

00:08:48.631 --> 00:08:51.616
We have the bluepoint
oysters, then crab claws.

00:08:51.616 --> 00:08:53.654
There is a Sterling
Brunch specialty omelet

00:08:53.654 --> 00:08:55.371
that Webster is famous for.

00:08:55.371 --> 00:08:57.407
It's lobster, boursin, and cognac.

00:08:57.407 --> 00:08:58.760
This is our carving station.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:01.919
We have the bacon, prime rib,
and lamb that's a staple.

00:09:01.919 --> 00:09:03.528
We have a variety of
pastries that are made

00:09:03.528 --> 00:09:05.015
by our in-house pastry chef.

00:09:05.015 --> 00:09:07.938
I personally always love
chocolate-covered strawberries.

00:09:07.938 --> 00:09:09.195
- How often is this brunch open?

00:09:09.195 --> 00:09:10.428
- It's open every Sunday.

00:09:10.428 --> 00:09:12.841
Being that it's one day a
week it makes it very easy

00:09:12.841 --> 00:09:14.206
for us to make sure that we're bringing

00:09:14.206 --> 00:09:16.206
the quality in as fresh as possible.

00:09:16.206 --> 00:09:17.314
- How much is the brunch?

00:09:17.314 --> 00:09:20.678
- It's $95, and that's the
all-you-can-have champagne

00:09:20.678 --> 00:09:23.043
included so it's definitely worth it.

00:09:23.043 --> 00:09:24.456
- Now it feels like we're in Vegas.

00:09:24.456 --> 00:09:27.554
Even the regular buffet food's elevated.

00:09:27.554 --> 00:09:30.371
Because everything here looks so good,

00:09:30.371 --> 00:09:32.176
we didn't make our own plates.

00:09:32.176 --> 00:09:34.857
We just got the best stuff and
we're going to share it all,

00:09:34.857 --> 00:09:37.367
in true worth-it form.

00:09:37.367 --> 00:09:41.343
- Hello, good morning, welcome
to the Sterling Brunch.

00:09:41.343 --> 00:09:43.743
Champagne wishes and caviar dreams.

00:09:43.743 --> 00:09:45.693
I'm Duff, I've been here for 18 years,

00:09:45.693 --> 00:09:46.911
started in 1998.

00:09:46.911 --> 00:09:48.220
- You got any good brunch stories?

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.414
- Favorite person you've ever waited on?

00:09:49.414 --> 00:09:50.723
- Rodney Dangerfield.

00:09:50.723 --> 00:09:51.946
That's how he was in real life.

00:09:51.946 --> 00:09:55.746
He would just come in and
was like hey, how's it going?

00:09:55.746 --> 00:09:56.778
- Thanks a lot for your service.

00:09:56.778 --> 00:09:59.171
Want to do some of this?

00:09:59.171 --> 00:10:00.878
(clinking)

00:10:00.878 --> 00:10:03.946
(piano music)

00:10:03.946 --> 00:10:06.481
- I love champagne, and the
sound of popping champagne.

00:10:06.481 --> 00:10:08.115
- Oh, here comes the buffet.

00:10:08.115 --> 00:10:09.495
Look at this popover.

00:10:09.495 --> 00:10:11.101
It kind of looks like an ice cream cone

00:10:11.101 --> 00:10:13.235
made of puff pastry.

00:10:13.235 --> 00:10:14.699
- Oh.
- Oh.

00:10:14.699 --> 00:10:16.235
- Whoa.
- Oh.

00:10:16.235 --> 00:10:19.652
(gentle classical music)

00:10:22.106 --> 00:10:23.605
- This is amazing.

00:10:23.605 --> 00:10:25.482
- I mean, this doesn't need butter.

00:10:25.482 --> 00:10:27.656
- Let's go to this egg.

00:10:27.656 --> 00:10:30.323
Lobster, cognac, boursin omelet.

00:10:35.507 --> 00:10:37.713
It's one of the stinkier cheeses,

00:10:37.713 --> 00:10:39.660
but with the butteriness of the lobster

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:41.323
it's really nice.

00:10:41.323 --> 00:10:45.292
- Do you want caviar, this
omelet, and make it even crazier?

00:10:45.292 --> 00:10:46.712
- Honestly, not really.

00:10:46.712 --> 00:10:49.795
(gentle piano music)

00:10:51.294 --> 00:10:52.476
- That's actually really good.

00:10:52.476 --> 00:10:53.500
The combination of ...

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:54.593
- All right, all right.

00:10:54.593 --> 00:10:58.193
(gentle piano music)

00:10:58.193 --> 00:11:00.508
- Ooh, all the sudden
there's like this sea breeze

00:11:00.508 --> 00:11:02.574
washing over the cheese.

00:11:02.574 --> 00:11:03.553
- It's like a puzzle.

00:11:03.553 --> 00:11:06.866
- It is a puzzle for your mouth to solve.

00:11:06.866 --> 00:11:07.848
Can I ask you another question?

00:11:07.848 --> 00:11:10.481
What was Mr. Dangerfield's
favorite thing to eat?

00:11:10.481 --> 00:11:12.270
- He was right at those lobster tails.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:14.490
- Well, I mean you've got
to do the lobster tails.

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:17.907
(gentle classical music)

00:11:20.977 --> 00:11:22.339
Is that your favorite thing so far?

00:11:22.339 --> 00:11:25.512
- It really is perfectly
cooked and so, so good.

00:11:25.512 --> 00:11:26.350
- Dessert time.

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:29.239
- She recommended
chocolate-covered strawberries.

00:11:29.239 --> 00:11:30.404
Can I get the white chocolate one?

00:11:30.404 --> 00:11:33.391
- White chocolate is for children.

00:11:33.391 --> 00:11:36.891
(ethereal choral singing)

00:11:40.746 --> 00:11:43.221
(laughs)

00:11:43.221 --> 00:11:44.672
- The strawberry's nice and tart.

00:11:44.672 --> 00:11:47.513
The chocolate dark and sweet,
the perfect strawberry.

00:11:47.513 --> 00:11:49.166
Yesterday you said that
you were going to bring

00:11:49.166 --> 00:11:51.184
your girlfriend into Wicked Spoon.

00:11:51.184 --> 00:11:53.205
This is where I'm bringing my girlfriend.

00:11:53.205 --> 00:11:55.536
Come on, we're in the desert in Nevada

00:11:55.536 --> 00:11:57.911
and I'm eating lobster from
the bottom of the ocean.

00:11:57.911 --> 00:12:00.487
- And there's no way it's
from yesterday's brunch

00:12:00.487 --> 00:12:02.490
because they only have it once a week.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.294
- Sterling Brunch, done?

00:12:05.294 --> 00:12:06.127
- Done.

00:12:12.064 --> 00:12:14.323
Guys, I'm intoxicated by
the sheer volume of food

00:12:14.323 --> 00:12:16.272
that we have consumed on this trip.

00:12:16.272 --> 00:12:18.476
- I'm more food drunk than
any other kind of drunk.

00:12:18.476 --> 00:12:19.828
- That's exactly what I just said.

00:12:19.828 --> 00:12:20.936
- I said it better.

00:12:20.936 --> 00:12:23.567
- So Andrew, Adam, what
did you guys think?

00:12:23.567 --> 00:12:27.054
What was the best buffet
at its given price point?

00:12:27.054 --> 00:12:29.434
- Red Rock was a ridiculous value.

00:12:29.434 --> 00:12:31.636
I don't know that I've
even eaten more food

00:12:31.636 --> 00:12:32.803
for less cost.

00:12:33.652 --> 00:12:37.439
That being said, that Sterling
Brunch was ridiculous.

00:12:37.439 --> 00:12:40.499
Duff in his tuxedo and his eye patch

00:12:40.499 --> 00:12:42.872
with his stories of Rodney Dangerfield,

00:12:42.872 --> 00:12:44.564
that's worth the price alone.

00:12:44.564 --> 00:12:46.911
My worth it winner, Sterling Brunch.

00:12:46.911 --> 00:12:48.374
I guess I'm a high roller now.

00:12:48.374 --> 00:12:49.556
- There's just a puppy strolling...

00:12:49.556 --> 00:12:50.738
- Oh my gosh.

00:12:50.738 --> 00:12:55.515
- Yo, pull the (bleep) over,
I'm petting this puppy.

00:12:55.515 --> 00:12:57.182
He's growling at me.

00:12:59.244 --> 00:13:01.161
He didn't want to play.

00:13:02.458 --> 00:13:06.594
- Red Rock, it was under $10,
and it was all of the classics

00:13:06.594 --> 00:13:08.500
that you wanted done well.

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:11.845
My worth the win today
goes to the Wicked Spoon.

00:13:11.845 --> 00:13:14.941
Everything was like a good
dish, plus something special.

00:13:14.941 --> 00:13:16.664
I would have liked vegetables
growing up as a kid

00:13:16.664 --> 00:13:18.001
if I ate his carrots.

00:13:18.001 --> 00:13:20.064
- Yeah, all kids should
be eating whiskey carrots.

00:13:20.064 --> 00:13:20.897
- Adam.

00:13:22.694 --> 00:13:23.777
- The winner?

00:13:28.626 --> 00:13:29.549
- Whoa.

00:13:29.549 --> 00:13:31.313
- You know what I'd like
to do an episode on?

00:13:31.313 --> 00:13:33.813
Little birds, pheasant, quail.

00:13:35.008 --> 00:13:37.058
- To eat or as pets?

00:13:37.058 --> 00:13:37.891
- To eat.

00:13:48.253 --> 00:13:49.575
- [Male] Oh yes.

